    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1658">

                <pb facs="1196" n="1080" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1080"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.6712/9.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State ad interim to the Chargé
                        d’Affaires of Turkey</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    copy of a despatch of the 1st instant from the American Consul at Aguascalientes
                    reporting that at the request of the firm of S. Bujdud Hermano and Jalife,
                    Ottoman subjects, he has obtained the release of ninety-four bales of cotton
                    which had been sequestered by the Mexican Government.</p>
                <p>I should be glad to be informed whether the Embassy has any advices concerning
                    the report contained in the despatch as to the designation of the German Consul
                    at San Luis Potosí to care for Ottoman interests.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
